flowchart TB
  accTitle: DorkOS systems and deployment boundaries
  accDescr: The client reaches the local execution server. Independent Community hosts serve multiple communities. Cloud hosting management is a planned HTTP connection to the host API, without content access. Marketplace discovery and installation use the same package sources.
  client["DorkOS client · React<br/>Browser / phone web app / desktop"]
  server["Local DorkOS server · Express<br/>Sessions · Rooms · Tasks · Relay · Mesh<br/>Local SQLite + files"]
  runtime["Local AgentRuntime implementations<br/>Claude Code · Codex · OpenCode<br/>Runtime-specific history"]
  cloud["Optional DorkOS Cloud<br/>Public hosted-service contract"]
  community["Independent Community host · Hono<br/>One or many communities<br/>Host sign-in · tenant memberships<br/>Own PostgreSQL + blob storage"]
  communityUI["Community browser · React"]
  sources["Marketplace sources<br/>Registries + package repositories"]
  site["DorkOS website · Next.js<br/>Docs + marketplace discovery"]
  client <-->|"HTTP commands / WebSocket events<br/>Community SSE"| server
  server -->|"SDK calls / local sidecar"| runtime
  server -->|"Optional HTTPS<br/>Link, heartbeat, managed services"| cloud
  server <-->|"Approved participation<br/>Qualified HTTP + SSE"| community
  cloud -.->|"Planned hosting management<br/>Host API; no content access"| community
  communityUI <-->|"HTTP commands / SSE events"| community
  server -->|"Fetch: HTTPS / Git / npm"| sources
  site -->|"HTTPS metadata + READMEs"| sources
  classDef service fill:#edf3fa,stroke:#46709b,color:#183047
  classDef hosted fill:#fff5e4,stroke:#a87720,color:#49320c
  class server,community,runtime,client,communityUI,site,sources service
  class cloud hosted
